                  <provenance type="#l" source="251"><orgName role="fmo" key="mlgbOrg_14">Abingdon, Berkshire.
                        Benedictine abbey of St Mary the Virgin</orgName><p>'Ded. eccl. Aben.' in
                        kalendar in red at 23 October. Arms of the abbey on a cross fleury between
                        four martlets sable at the foot of the first page of the
                     Breviarium.</p></provenance>
                  <provenance type="MLGB3_laterOwners">Richard Lofthouse Richard Bartlett gave to
                     All Souls, Oxford</provenance>
               <provenance type="#e" source="4278"><orgName role="fmo" key="mlgbOrg_425">Oxford, Oxfordshire.
                        All Souls' College</orgName><p>Erased inscr. legible by u. v. light:
                        'Liber collegii animarum omnium fidelium defunctorum in Oxonia ex dono
                        venerabilis viri Ricardi Bartlett in medicinis doctor et quondam huius
                        collegii socii' (s. xvi), at foot of 2nd leaf of the breviarium (fol. 12r).
                        Earlier at Abingdon, q. v.</p><p>Excluded from MLGB Suppl. (1987) since not
                        sure is All Souls until 1551.</p></provenance>
